  "majd": {"fr": "« Gloire, splendeur » en arabe, dérivé de مجد (majada), « être glorieux ».", "en": "Means \"glory, splendour\" in Arabic, a derivative of مجد (majada) meaning \"to be glorious\".", "url": "https://www.behindthename.com/name/majd", "refs": ["Wehr, Hans. A Dictionary of Modern Written Arabic. Spoken Language Services, 1979, page 1049."]},
  "majdi": {"fr": "« Glorieux, digne d’éloges » en arabe, de la racine مجد (majada), « être glorieux ».", "en": "Means \"glorious, praiseworthy\" in Arabic, from the root مجد (majada) meaning \"to be glorious\".", "url": "https://www.behindthename.com/name/majdi", "refs": ["Wehr, Hans. A Dictionary of Modern Written Arabic. Spoken Language Services, 1979, page 1049."]},
  "majid": {"fr": "« Glorieux, magnifique » en arabe, de la racine مجد (majada), « être glorieux ».", "en": "Means \"glorious, magnificent\" in Arabic, from the root مجد (majada) meaning \"to be glorious\".", "url": "https://www.behindthename.com/name/majid", "refs": ["Wehr, Hans. A Dictionary of Modern Written Arabic. Spoken Language Services, 1979, page 1049."]},
